amentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Ron DeSantis (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Florida's governor's race is an open-seat contest between Republican Byron Donalds and Democrat David Jolly, a former Republican congressman now running as a Democrat, with several minor candidates on the ballot. The state's rightward tilt gives Donalds the starting advantage, and he has built a clear financial edge with nearly $14 million raised.\n\nPolling through mid-October consistently shows Donalds ahead, with averages clustering around four to five points and a late Stetson poll putting him in double digits. Prediction markets price his chances near 80 percent, and most race raters call the contest Lean Republican. Jolly's path runs through moderate voters and undecided Black Floridians, and headlines show him courting both, but Democratic groups have not yet invested heavily in the state. The race is competitive but tilts Republican with three weeks to go.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1709, "margin": -5.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2654, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2923, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2636, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1983, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2414, "margin": -3.8}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2597, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2217, "margin": -4.8}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2584, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.252, "margin": -4.3}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2745, "margin": -3.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2552, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2498, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2281, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2329, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2195, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2688, "margin": -3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2284, "